<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore March non-oil exports fall 2.1 pct on yr. [corrected 11:01 gmt]</title>
<headline>Singapore March non-oil exports fall 2.1 pct on yr. [corrected 11:01 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 2.1 percent year-on-year in March to Singapore $7.67 billion after falling 7.9 percent in February, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports rose (corrects from fell) 0.5 percent in March to S$9.88 billion after falling 4.4 percent in February.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of 11 economists last week had forecast a 4.5 percent drop in the nominal figure.  </p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				   March		 February</p>
<p>    Total trade	   32.35 (0.8)	   24.24 (-8.7)</p>
<p>    Exports		 15.50 (-1.0)	  11.60 (-6.2)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports     8.97 (-4.2)	   6.72 (-7.4)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.29(-15.0)	   1.21 (-4.8)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  7.67 (-2.1)	   5.52 (-7.9)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     6.54 (3.7)	    4.86 (-4.4)</p>
<p>    Imports		 16.85 (2.6)	   12.64(-11.0)</p>
<p>Trade in real terms, in blns of S$ at 1990 prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage change given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				   March		 February</p>
<p>    Total trade	   38.63 (3.3)	   28.91 (-6.2)</p>
<p>    Exports		 19.14 (1.0)	   14.31 (-3.7)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports    11.68 (-2.9)	   8.75 (-5.8)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.80(-18.1)	   1.62(-11.5)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  9.88 (0.5)	    7.12 (-4.4)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     7.46 (7.7)	    5.57 (-0.2)</p>
<p>    Imports		 19.50 (5.6)	   14.60 (-8.5)</p>
<p>Singapore's major markets for non-oil domestic exports in nominal terms (at current prices) in billions of S$.</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes in parentheses)</p>
<p>				   March		  February</p>
<p>    U.S.		     2.09(-11.9)	   1.52(-11.8)</p>
<p>    EU			 1.56 (15.2)	   1.13 (-7.2)</p>
<p>    Malaysia		 1.04 (11.2)	   0.68 (-1.7)</p>
<p>    Japan		    0.61(-24.7)	   0.47(-23.0)</p>
<p>    Hong Kong		0.51 (-9.5)	   0.29 (-4.3)</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
